# Architecture

## Overview

{{ project_name }} is a TypeScript agent application using {{ agent_framework }}{% if execution_model != "cli" %} with a {% if execution_model == "web" %}Next.js{% else %}Hono{% endif %} backend{% endif %}.

## Project Structure

```
src/
  agents/              # Agent definitions
    example.ts         # Example agent ({{ agent_framework }})
  tools/               # Agent tools/functions
{%- if execution_model == "cli" %}
  index.ts             # CLI entry point (commander)
  commands/            # CLI subcommands
{%- elif execution_model == "service" %}
  index.ts             # Bun server entry point
  app.ts               # Hono app factory
  telemetry.ts         # OpenTelemetry setup
  routers/             # HTTP endpoint definitions
    health.ts          # /healthz, /readyz
  controllers/         # Request orchestration
  dtos/                # Zod request/response schemas
{%- elif execution_model == "web" %}
  app/                 # Next.js App Router
  components/          # React components
  hooks/               # Custom React hooks
  lib/                 # Utilities and configuration
{%- endif %}
  config.ts            # zod-based env/config validation
  logging.ts           # pino setup
  services/            # Business logic
{%- if include_clients %}
  clients/             # External API/service clients
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database %}
  db.ts                # Prisma client setup
  repositories/        # Data access layer
{%- endif %}
tests/
  unit/                # Fast, isolated unit tests
  integration/         # Tests with real dependencies
  e2e/                 # End-to-end tests
```
{% if execution_model == "cli" %}
## Flow

```
CLI commands (parse args, call agents)
  -> agents ({{ agent_framework }}, orchestrate tools)
    -> tools (functions the agent can call)
    -> services (business logic)
{%- if include_clients %}
      -> clients (external API calls)
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database %}
      -> repositories (data access)
{%- endif %}
```
{% else %}
## Layering

```
routers (HTTP endpoints, validate with zod)
  -> controllers (orchestrate across services/agents)
    -> agents ({{ agent_framework }}, orchestrate tools)
      -> tools (functions the agent can call)
    -> services (business logic)
{%- if include_clients %}
      -> clients (external API calls)
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database %}
      -> repositories (data access via Prisma)
{%- endif %}
```

DTOs (zod schemas) are used at the router and controller level for API I/O. They are always separate from database models.
{% endif %}
